  "title": "Rumi (Jalal al-Din Rumi)",
  "summary": "Rumi (1207–1273), poet and teacher, was born in Vakhsh (now Tajikistan) according to Encyclopedia.com, though World History Encyclopedia says Balkh. His family left eastern Persia by about 1216 and settled in Anatolia, and by 1229 his father taught in Konya. Rumi met Shams al-Din Tabrizi in 1244 and began the Masnavi, about 25,000 lines, around 1262. The Mevlevi order, known for whirling, grew from his poetry.",
